    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        30,
        800
      ],
      "size": [
        430,
        172
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 2,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "🛈 SDXL/Illustrious inpaint pipeline v2: Inpaint Crop zooms into the masked region (with context + feathered mask), the crop is sampled at full resolution with InpaintModelConditioning + Differential Diffusion, then Inpaint Stitch pastes the result losslessly back into the original image.\n\nWe dropped the Fooocus inpaint patch from v1 — combining it with Differential Diffusion double-applies masking and caused the color blotching / weak prompt adherence you saw. Differential Diffusion alone (with a feathered mask) is the more reliable technique for a non-inpaint-trained checkpoint.\n\n[Background on this workflow](https://comfyanonymous.github.io/ComfyUI_examples/inpaint/)"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 36,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        480,
        800
      ],
      "size": [
        430,
        207
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 3,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "⚠️ Requires the **ComfyUI-Inpaint-CropAndStitch** custom node pack (lquesada) via ComfyUI Manager. No extra model downloads needed.\n\nAfter installing, open the ✂️ Inpaint Crop node and set:\n- mode → \"forced size\"\n- force_width / force_height → 1024 (or your preferred SDXL aspect, e.g. 832x1216)\n\nThis makes the crop always get resized up to full SDXL resolution before sampling, no matter how small the painted mask is — this is what fixes low-detail/blotchy results on small masked regions. Leaving mode on \"free size\" will sample at whatever the raw crop size happens to be, which can be far below SDXL's native resolution."
      ],
      "color": "#333",
      "bgcolor": "#555"
    },
